/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:131:Scale a minority cell's inner pattern up to the cell-grid level, completing a fractal overlay.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:132:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:133:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:134:- Grid divided into NxN cells by separator lines of a single color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:135:- Most cells share an identical interior pattern (majority); a few have a distinct pattern (minority).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:136:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:137:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:138:- Extract the inner pixel pattern from the minority cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:139:- Treat each pixel as a cell-sized stamp: active pixels → minority pattern, inactive → majority pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:140:- Position this scaled-up pattern on the cell grid so existing minority cells align with active pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:141:- Fill in all remaining active positions with the minority pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:142:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:143:Key insight: The minority cell's interior is a miniature blueprint of where minority cells should appear at the grid scale — fractal self-similarity.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:144:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:145:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:146:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:147:<reference_puzzle index="9" source="eval" puzzle_id="89565ca0" lines="120-136">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:148:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:149:Convert each colored partitioned frame into a horizontal bar whose length is its number of enclosed regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:150:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:151:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:152:- Black background with several axis-aligned colored line drawings.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:153:- The line drawings are damaged by scattered pixels of one non-background noise color and by overlaps with other drawings.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:154:- Each real drawing is a rectangular partitioned frame enclosing one or more background regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:155:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:156:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:157:- For each non-background color, reconstruct its horizontal and vertical wall segments from dense row/column evidence.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:158:- Count the 4-connected background regions fully enclosed by those reconstructed walls.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:159:- The color with no enclosed region is the noise/pad color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:160:- Sort drawing colors by enclosed-region count; equal counts are ordered by which reconstructed frame covers the other.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:161:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:162:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:163:- The scattered color is not an object; it only pads the histogram, while each true object's room count is stable after rectilinear wall reconstruction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:164:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:165:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:166:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:167:<reference_puzzle index="10" source="eval" puzzle_id="13e47133" lines="56-69">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:168:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:169:Fill partitioned regions with concentric colored bands derived from marker pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:170:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:171:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:172:- Grid partitioned into regions by wall-colored lines.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:173:- Each region has a dominant base color and a few isolated marker pixels of other colors at varying depths from the region boundary.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:174:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:175:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:176:- For each region, read marker colors ordered by their Chebyshev distance from the boundary to build a color palette.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:177:- If no marker sits on the boundary itself, the base color leads the palette.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:178:- Paint every cell with palette[distance mod palette_length], producing repeating concentric rectangular frames that radiate inward.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:179:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:180:Key insight: Each marker's depth from the boundary defines its position in the cyclic palette; the pattern then tiles inward automatically.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:181:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:182:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:183:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:184:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="eval" puzzle_id="a25697e4" lines="9-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:185:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:186:Dock movable tools into border-anchored frames by filling cavities.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:187:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:188:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:189:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:190:- Border-touching components cluster into anchor frames with interior bg cavities.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:191:- Non-border 2-color components are movable tools.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:192:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:193:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:194:- Match each tool to a frame whose cavity size equals one of its color-region counts.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:195:- Rotate/flip the tool so one color fills the cavity exactly; the other stays outside.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:196:- If the docking orientation uses a reflection, swap the tool's two colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:197:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:198:Key insight: Cavity size determines tool–frame pairing; reflection triggers color swap.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:199:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:200:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:201:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:202:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="eval" puzzle_id="7666fa5d" lines="12-26">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:203:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:204:Fill the parallelogram-shaped region between parallel anti-diagonal line segments with red.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:205:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:206:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:207:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:208:- One non-bg color forms short diagonal segments, each lying on a single anti-diagonal (r+c = const).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:209:- Segments come in parallel pairs bounding a region to be filled.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:210:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:211:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:212:- For each main-diagonal axis (r−c = const), collect anti-diagonal segments whose span covers that axis.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:213:- Sort those segments by their anti-diagonal index (r+c).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:214:- Fill all bg cells lying strictly between consecutive segment pairs along that axis with red (color 2).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:215:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:216:Key insight: The two diagonal directions decouple — segments sit on anti-diagonals, and filling sweeps along main diagonals between them, forming parallelogram regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:217:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:218:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:219:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:220:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="eval" puzzle_id="16de56c4" lines="9-34">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:221:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:222:Fill periodic progressions that shoot from a unique grid edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:223:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:224:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:225:- bg = most common color.  Sparse non-bg dots of several colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:226:- All repeating colors originate from the same grid edge (top, bottom,
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:227:  left, or right — the one with the most non-bg dots).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:228:- Each repeating color has exactly 2 dots per shooting-direction line;
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:229:  their gap defines the step.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:230:- Every non-bg dot lies on a shooting-direction line that contains a
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:231:  repeating color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:232:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:233:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:234:- Determine the unique shooting edge; left/right → rows, top/bottom → columns.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:235:- For each shooting-direction line, the repeating color has exactly 2 dots;
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:236:  step = gap between them, offset = first position mod step.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:237:- A different-colored dot aligned to the same beat (pos % step == offset) is
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:238:  a companion: it absorbs the ray and becomes the fill color, limiting the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:239:  fill range to the span between repeating and companion dots.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:240:- An unaligned dot is a bystander and left untouched.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:241:- Without a companion the repeating color fills the entire line.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:242:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:243:Key insight: the shooting edge is identified by counting boundary dots;
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:244:the gap between the two marker dots is the period; a companion sharing the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:245:modular class acts as a wall that stops the ray and dictates the paint color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:246:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:247:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:248:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:249:<reference_puzzle index="14" source="eval" puzzle_id="8b7bacbf" lines="42-56">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:250:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:251:Fill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:252:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:253:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:254:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:255:- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:256:- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:257:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:258:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:259:- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:260:- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:261:- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:262:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:263:Key insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:264:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:265:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:266:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:267:<reference_puzzle index="15" source="eval" puzzle_id="e87109e9" lines="68-83">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:268:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:269:Emit four teal beams from a square, turning at colored obstacles per a legend.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:270:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:271:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:272:- Top band: grey (5) legend with colored vertical bars in cells; bar position (left or right) encodes turn direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:273:- Below: main grid with bg, a solid teal (8) square, and colored obstacle blocks.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:274:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:275:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:276:- Remove the legend from the output.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:277:- From the teal square, shoot a beam in each cardinal direction (as a sliding copy of the square).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:278:- Each beam paints teal over bg cells as it moves.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:279:- On hitting an obstacle of color C, consult the legend: bar on left → turn counterclockwise, bar on right → turn clockwise. Continue in the new direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:280:- Beams stop at grid edges.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:281:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:282:Key insight: The legend's bar position (left vs right within its cell) is the encoding for turn direction at each obstacle color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:283:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:284:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:285:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:286:<reference_puzzle index="16" source="eval" puzzle_id="271d71e2" lines="9-22">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:287:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:288:Move bordered containers toward same-colored destination markers, charging gray cells to orange.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:289:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:290:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:291:- bg = 6 (magenta). Black-bordered (0) rectangles with gray (5) / orange (7) interiors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:292:- A head sprite (9) sits adjacent to one container edge; a matching destination sprite lies along the movement axis.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:293:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:294:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:295:- Each container translates toward its destination along the head-to-dest axis.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:296:- Steps = min(head-to-dest distance, number of gray interior cells).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:297:- Gray cells become orange from the head-facing side inward, one per step.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:298:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:299:Key insight: Gray cell count caps movement — a container stops short if it runs out of gray cells to charge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:300:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:301:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:302:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:303:<reference_puzzle index="17" source="eval" puzzle_id="b10624e5" lines="24-39">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:304:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:305:Replicate a motif across quadrants with scaling and reflection keyed to red anchor blocks.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:306:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:307:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:308:- Grid divided into four quadrants by a full-row and full-column divider of a single non-bg color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:309:- Each quadrant contains a red (2) square anchor block of varying size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:310:- The top-left quadrant also has a colored motif attached to its red anchor.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:311:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:312:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:313:- Use the top-left quadrant's motif as the source pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:314:- For each other quadrant, scale the motif by the ratio of that quadrant's red block size to the source red block size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:315:- Reflect horizontally for right-side quadrants, vertically for bottom quadrants (both for bottom-right).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:316:- Align the scaled/reflected motif so its red region overlaps the target anchor, then stamp non-bg pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:317:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:318:Key insight: Red block size encodes the scale factor; quadrant position encodes the reflection axes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:319:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:320:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:321:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:322:<reference_puzzle index="18" source="eval" puzzle_id="5961cc34" lines="8-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:323:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:324:Build a red ray network by activating blue blobs via directional green ports.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:325:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:326:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:327:- bg = most common color. Large blue blobs with adjacent green pixels marking port directions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:328:- Start marker: yellow pixel atop a short red segment at grid bottom.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:329:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed90943981/2/prompt.md:330:Rule:
